    "label": "Helping guest with child and milk",
    "quote": "I helped her take her luggage up to the room, and saw her rummaging in her bag for formula, so I went down to the convenience store, bought a carton of milk, warmed it up in hot water and took it up to her."
  },
  {
    "label": "Downplaying the praise as routine",
    "quote": "Honestly, anyone would have done the same in that situation. There’s nothing special about it. You don’t need to put it in specially."
  },
  {
    "label": "Team reaction to praise",
    "quote": "My team leader read out my name at the morning briefing, everyone clapped, and then we moved straight on to assigning that day’s airport pick-ups."
  },
  {
    "label": "Focus on appraisal criteria over recognition",
    "quote": "What I care about more is the appraisal at the end of the month. That’s mainly based on luggage errors and punctuality."
  },
  {
    "label": "Hotel's regular practice of displaying praise letters",
    "quote": "Our hotel puts up a dozen or so every month, for the front desk, housekeeping and concierge, and some people get three or four a month, so nobody makes much of them."
  },
  {
    "label": "Personal life unrelated to the praise letter",
    "quote": "That evening I phoned my mum. Mostly we talked about her coming to visit me next month: which day’s train to book, where she’d stay. We talked for almost an hour, and I actually forgot to mention it."
  }
],
